module

public import TauCeti.Algebra.AlgebraicGroup.Reductive.Basic
public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.E6.DoubledMinuscule.Generated.Connected
public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.E6.DoubledMinuscule.Generated.UnipotentRadical

/-!
# Reductivity of the subgroup generated by the doubled type-E₆ roots and torus

Over every field, the closed subgroup of `GL₅₄` generated by the twelve numbered root subgroups
and the weight torus of the doubled minuscule carrier `V(ϖ₁) ⊕ V(ϖ₆)` is reductive. The generated
subgroup is smooth and geometrically connected. Over an algebraic closure its faithful completely
reducible standard representation rules out nontrivial connected normal smooth unipotent
subgroups.

Generation commutes with free field extension
(`TauCeti.E6DoubledMinuscule.generatedCoordinateHopfAlgebraBaseChangeIso`), so the subgroup
generated over the algebraic closure is the geometric fibre used in the reductivity criterion.

This result concerns the group generated over the field. The base change of the integral
toral-closure carrier contains it, but the two are not identified here, and neither is identified
with the pinned simply connected group scheme of type `E₆`; constructions on the generated
subgroup transfer to that group only along such an identification.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.E6DoubledMinuscule.reductiveCommHopfAlgProperty_generatedCoordinateHopfAlgebra`: the
  generated subgroup is reductive over every field.

## References

* J. S. Milne, *Algebraic Groups* (2017), §2.h and Chapter 19.
* J. E. Humphreys, *Linear Algebraic Groups*, §§19 and 26.
* J. C. Jantzen, *Representations of Algebraic Groups*, I.2 and II.2.

The argument follows the generated tripled type-`D₄` subgroup in
`TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.D4.Tripled.Generated.Reductive`.
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory

namespace TauCeti.E6DoubledMinuscule

universe u

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-- **The subgroup generated by the doubled type-`E₆` roots and torus is reductive over every
field.** The closed subgroup of `GL₅₄` generated over `k` by the numbered root subgroups and the
weight torus of the doubled minuscule carrier is smooth and geometrically connected, with no
nontrivial connected normal smooth unipotent closed subgroup after extension to an algebraic
closure. -/
theorem reductiveCommHopfAlgProperty_generatedCoordinateHopfAlgebra :
    reductiveCommHopfAlgProperty k
      (FiniteTypeCommHopfAlgCat.of k (generatedCoordinateHopfAlgebra k)) := by
  let K := AlgebraicClosure k
  let e := generatedCoordinateHopfAlgebraBaseChangeIso.{u, u} k K
  exact reductiveCommHopfAlgProperty_of_geometricFiber_iso_of_smooth_connected k _
    (FiniteTypeCommHopfAlgCat.of K (generatedCoordinateHopfAlgebra K))
    (ObjectProperty.isoMk _ e) (smoothCommHopfAlgProperty_generatedCoordinateHopfAlgebra K)
    (geometricallyConnectedCommHopfAlgProperty_generatedCoordinateHopfAlgebra K)
    (eq_augmentation_generated_of_isNormal_of_smoothUnipotent K)

end TauCeti.E6DoubledMinuscule
